# playpick cell: mode=walk boss=gift spec=shaman:restoration style=melee
# size=25 difficulty=heroic view=1280x800 save=carried.
#
# save=carried behaves as fresh here -- #273, still open: playbot's PID-
# derived port gives every invocation a fresh localStorage origin, so
# --profile never actually carries anything between separate playbot runs.
# So this follows the same recipe every other 25-heroic walk/clear cell in
# this ledger has used since 2026-09-26: `open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1` to unlock
# the rung, then back out to a real front-door RAID -> WALK IN.
#
# `boss=gift` is a coverage label only (direction.md's running note on
# mode=walk): `evening` steers at no boss, so this starts at the door same
# as any other walk. gift (The Crimson Gift) sits at room `sanctum`,
# encounter 7, reached threshold -> vigil -> spire(marrow,0) -> climb ->
# oratory(whisper,1) -> mooring(encounter 10) -> rise(gorged,3) -> crossing
# -> crimson(crowns,6) -> sanctum(gift,7) -- six raid fights and seven
# corridor hops away, read off src/dungeon.ts's ROOMS/DOORS tables. Given
# how this ledger's last nine #271/[[#6]] confirmations have gone, reaching
# gift itself is not the likely outcome of this script; the corridor is.
#
# Checked sessions.jsonl first: shaman:restoration has been played seven
# times before this (raid/daily/clear/battleground) and never once inside
# mode=walk -- this is its first evening, full stop. style=melee +
# 25-heroic + carried + boss=gift is the exact shape 2026-09-28-23.play
# already ran on priest:discipline (eighth #271/[[#6]] confirmation,
# wiped in THE VIGIL at 39.6s, stuck at 100.6s) -- the new axis here is the
# spec. shaman's moveSpeed is 167 (src/sim/classes.ts), same tier as
# druid:restoration and mage:frost, both of which still got caught by the
# corridor's watchmen under `mash`/`auto`/`flee` despite not being the
# slowest class in the roster -- so this also tests whether a 167-speed
# healer under `melee` specifically (beelines at hud().boss, no
# away-from-danger term) fares any differently than the 158-speed
# priest:discipline did on the identical style/size/difficulty/save/boss
# shape, or lands on the same wall regardless.
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:shaman:restoration
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start
targets
ui
evening melee 200 10
shot end
state
says
bill
